### Task G — `docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md` (MODIFY)

Add a new subsection at §12 (federation-primitive integration appendix) titled `### 12.8 Break-glass procedure for federation-primitive failure`. Place it immediately after §12.7.15 (Cross-repo scorecard opt-in). Before §13.

Content: 3-gate playbook for the scenario where SCP's federation primitive ships a defect (Rego syntax error, supply-chain compromise, etc.) and adopters need to temporarily bypass the gate without manually mutating branch protection from the GitHub UI.

Gate 1 (DISABLE): operator runs `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <captured-pre-state.json>` to revert the target adopter's branch protection from the captured before-state in the original invocation log entry. The pre-state JSON is at the bottom of every invocation log block per `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` format; copy it to a local file first. SLO: <30 min from operator decision to restored state.

Gate 2 (FIX): operator pins the SCP federation-primitive wrapper SHA in the adopter's `policy-check-wrapper.yml` to the last known-good release tag (e.g. `v1.2.0` SHA `5d4341b...`). This is a sibling PR on the adopter repo; merge per adopter-side review.

Gate 3 (RE-ENABLE): once the SCP federation primitive ships a fix release tag (`v1.2.1`+), Renovate auto-PRs the SHA bump in the adopter repo. Operator re-runs `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo <owner/repo> --branch <branch>` to re-arm the required-check after Renovate-bump-PR merges + observed clean.

Rationale paragraph: this break-glass is the rollback SLO claimed by WP-SCP-024 plan-doc invariant 7 (single-operator-doable + <30 min from decision to merge-restored state). The gate is intentionally 3-step (not a one-button kill-switch) because (a) every gate is auditable in git history; (b) Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; (c) Gate 3 ensures the adopter doesn't stay un-gated forever.

Reference line at end: `Reference: WP-SCP-024 plan-doc invariant 7; D-044 (slice 024B); D-035 (operator-run + invocation-logged); enable-required-check.sh --restore mode; ADOPT-001 §12.7 federation-primitive adoption.`

