g-effort medium) — implementation: scaffolder + template + `--restore` extension + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests + ADOPT-001 §12 break-glass + D-044 row + STATUS.md update. Capture work-package + stdout to `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/codex-dispatch-manual-audit.log`.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:125:7. **Operator real-repo `--restore` round-trip demo** (operator-interactive; standard `gh` PAT; throw-away test repo). Evidence captured into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md`. Demo blocks slice merge per plan-doc §6 acceptance criterion + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:126:8. **Self-merge** per D-040 single-operator-mode after fixpoint + CI green + `--restore` demo evidence committed.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:136:| 2 | Codex executor (direct `codex exec`): scaffolder + template + `--restore` + CI script + unit tests + ADOPT-001 §12 + D-044 row + STATUS.md | Codex T3 deviated | ~45–60 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:140:| 6 | `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo on throw-away test repo | Operator-interactive `gh` calls | ~15 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:151:Per `docs/DECISIONS.md` header, D-044 is reserved for this slice. Codex executor MUST NOT assign D-044 to any other decision filed during this slice. The reservation pattern mirrors D-021 (WP-SCP-022) + D-041–043 (WP-SCP-023) + D-044/045/046 (WP-SCP-024 reservation block already in place).\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-03 (D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A; estate cascade)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 is reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:33:> --restore` rollback mode). D-045 is reserved for slice 024C (estate\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:43:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:82:| D-035 | 2026-04-30 | Adopt the WP-SCP-020 slice 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine. The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate). Adopters of the SCP federation primitive enable this required status check on their default branch via `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` from the SCP repo. The script applies branch protection in two API calls (unified PUT for status-checks/admins/reviews + dedicated POST to `required_signatures` sub-resource per the GitHub API shape), refuses to bypass admin enforcement without an explicit `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` acknowledgement flag, refuses to run in CI (CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true env-var guards), preserves any pre-existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it, and emits an invocation-log block (operator, timestamp, script SHA256 + git SHA, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON) for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure: an apply without the log entry is considered unrecorded. Estate cascade rollout (WP-SCP-024) drives this script across PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower; FLA pilot (WP-SCP-020.1) is the canary first invocation | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection), D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account), D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-status-check), D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection): every operational procedure that mutates third-party repository state ships an idempotent applier + ratifying D-NNN + invocation log convention. The bootstrap-only / no-CI guard reflects that this script writes to a third-party repo's branch protection — an automation tool that ran it unattended could mass-mutate the estate via stolen credentials before any operator noticed. The `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` confirmation reflects that `--no-enforce-admins` defeats the whole point of the federation primitive on the target repo and so should require explicit intent. The `required_pull_request_reviews` preservation reflects that adopters with multi-maintainer teams have legitimate review-shape state that 020G must not destroy. Identified at WP-SCP-020 §4 020G + 020G R1 review (3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 2 nit on safety, 2 MAJ + 4 MIN + nit on completeness, 3 MAJ + 2 MIN + 2 nit on correctness — fixpoint via fix-round-1) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:90:| D-043 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report (`docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D (this PR). Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` produces deterministic golden-file-tested output reading `output/scorecards/index.json`; aggregator workflow `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` extended in the commit job to invoke the generator + add the rendered markdown to the operator-review PR alongside the index. MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (registered in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py`): read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5; request shape `{repo_filter?, since_emitted_at?}`; response shape excludes waiver content (`reason` / `approved_by` / `waiver_id` — invariant 2) by Pydantic model construction (extra=forbid + explicit field whitelist). The MCP method reads `output/scorecards/index.json` from the SCP repo working copy at call time; staleness is observable via the response's `aggregated_at` field. ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by Pydantic models + schema + dedicated pytest scans on both markdown + MCP responses) | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 + D-042 — D-043 ratifies the CONSUMER side: markdown for operators/auditors, MCP for agents/tooling. Read-only contract + Pydantic-enforced field whitelist + golden-file pytest together preserve invariant 2 across both surfaces. The MCP method does NOT introduce a new authentication primitive — it rides on WP-SCP-021's existing Ed25519 receipt mechanism (consult-class semantics). The markdown report is informational and CODEOWNERS-protected via `docs/scorecards/** @jrnb2024`; operators can hand-edit before merging the aggregator PR if needed (regenerator overwrites on next run). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the MCP server runs at acc.brokapps.ai; if down, agents lose `consult_scorecard` access but the markdown report + git index remain consultable. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation |\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:32:#     `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` and merge.\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:436:LOG_FILE=\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:861:7. Emits an invocation-log markdown block for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` on the SCP repo. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1128:#### 12.7.15 Cross-repo scorecard opt-in (post-WP-SCP-023 / v1.2.0)\nSTATUS.md:3:**Last updated:** 2026-05-09 (D-035-rules retired under 2026-05-15 deadline; WP-SCP-025 parked; previous: 2026-05-03 slice 020Q)\nSTATUS.md:49:## Today's chain (2026-04-30 — single session)\nSTATUS.md:71:## Today's chain (2026-05-01 — post-Threshold-A session)\nSTATUS.md:86:## Today's chain (2026-05-02 — full backlog clear + first rule-RFC dogfood)\nSTATUS.md:110:## Today's chain (2026-05-03 — WP-SCP-023 closed at Threshold A scaffolding + WP-SCP-024 opens)\nSTATUS.md:117:| 4 | #100 | **023D** | Cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (closes D-043). NEW `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested output; reads `output/scorecards/index.json` → `docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`). Aggregator workflow extended (commit job invokes generator + adds markdown to operator-review PR). NEW MCP method `consult_scorecard` in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py` with read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, NEVER waiver content per invariant 2). NEW `tests/scorecard-report/` (3 golden fixtures × 2 tests = 7) + `tests/scp_mcp/test_tools/test_consult_scorecard.py` (9 tests including waiver-content scan). NEW ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 — adopter onboarding workflow (opt-in PR, privacy contract, MCP usage, 4 common failure modes table). 51/51 pytest pass. Internal-only delta to aggregator workflow; MCP method addition is additive (registered tool name only) so no federation primitive version bump per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\". |\nSTATUS.md:119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:121:## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — D-035-rules retired + WP-SCP-025 parked)\nSTATUS.md:137:**Slice 024B remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope unchanged: scaffolder + `--restore` mode + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + D-044 + real-repo rollback round-trip.\nSTATUS.md:225:- **TF-023C-001** (medium priority): SCP self-dogfood — opt the SCP repo's own `policy-check-wrapper.yml` self-test into `scorecard-emit: true` so the aggregator has a 1-adopter test corpus before real adopters arrive. Target slice 023E (or earlier).\nSTATUS.md:238:- **TF-023E-002** (medium priority): SCP-self wrapper SHA pin is **stuck at v1.0.0 (@41a5299)** — bumping to any post-WP-SCP-023 SHA produces `startup_failure` because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation) against the caller's ceiling. The `attest-scorecard` job in `policy-check.yml@5ff2acd` declares `attestations: write` + `id-token: write`, which exceeds the wrapper's `contents:read + statuses:write` ceiling, even when `scorecard-emit: false` would skip the job at runtime. Closure path: (a) restructure `policy-check.yml` so `attest-scorecard` lives in a separate top-level workflow file (called workflows can't have job-scoped perms above caller ceiling regardless of `if:`), OR (b) once TF-023E-001 unblocks (repo public/org-owned), grant `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` universally at the wrapper level. (a) preserves least-privilege for opt-out adopters and is the recommended path. Surfaced at 023E fix-round-3 (the bumped wrapper failed startup_failure even after reverting `scorecard-emit: true` because the SHA bump alone trips the validation). Real adopters that opt in MUST follow the (b) path because they will universally grant the two permissions per ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 step 2.\nSTATUS.md:254:- **D-035 (2026-04-30)** — 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` two-call PUT + POST shape, refuses CI, preserves `required_pull_request_reviews`, mandatory invocation-log commit at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`.\nSTATUS.md:262:- **D-043 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D. Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested). MCP method has read-only contract per plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, never waiver content per invariant 2; Pydantic-enforced field whitelist). ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. Closes plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:10:- **D-044** — reserved for slice 024B: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder`) operational contract + adopter-template versioning + invocation-log convention extension.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:30:2. Defines a **per-adopter onboarding contract** that each cascade slice satisfies: (a) caller wrapper PR'd into the adopter repo with SCP federation primitive SHA-pinned per VERSIONING.md (D-036); (b) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` invocation per D-035 with invocation-log entry under `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` — **conditional on the slice's `cascade-status:` declaration per §5.2 + invariant 2** (only `onboarded` and `onboarded-operator-bump` slices add a log entry; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` slices MUST NOT modify the log file); (c) post-bake observation window of ≥1 calendar week before cascade declares the adopter onboarded; (d) opt-in scorecard-emit added as a follow-up sub-slice once TF-023E-002 closes AND the adopter's repo visibility allows OIDC artefact attestation per TF-023E-001.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:31:3. Defines a **canary-first sequencing** that minimises blast radius: smallest cooperative adopter first (PIM target), control-tower (high-traffic flagship) second, then mapp-doc-agent + recommender as a paired slice, then shopify-app last. The sequencing is reversible per slice — any adopter can be removed via PR to the adopter wrapper file + a parallel `enable-required-check.sh --restore` invocation (added at slice 024B).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:32:4. Defines a **scaffolder helper** (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` = `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) that emits the adopter-side artefacts (wrapper + CODEOWNERS template + ADOPT-001 reference) from a versioned template, so each cascade slice's adopter PR is mechanically consistent.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:44:2. **Required-check enablement is operator-run + invocation-logged + CI-enforced.** `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` per D-035 runs from the operator's local environment (the script refuses CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true per D-035), with an invocation log entry under `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` (the D-035-canonical estate-cascade audit trail; the file's existing comment \"Estate cascade rollout = WP-SCP-024\" reserves it for this WP) that captures operator, timestamp, script SHA256, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON. An apply without the log entry is unrecorded. **CI enforcement (lands in 024B as `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh`)** parses DISPATCH-NOTE `cascade-status:` field. **Fail-closed default (closes 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-003 safety):** if `cascade-status:` is absent OR contains a value not in the enumerated set `{onboarded, onboarded-operator-bump, blocked-on-adopter-conflict}`, the script exits non-zero (CI fails). Recognised values map to check-paths:\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:45:   - **`cascade-status: onboarded` (Renovate path):** PR MUST modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` AND the modified entry's target repo string MUST match the DISPATCH-NOTE's target.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:46:   - **`cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump` (R-024-07 fallback path):** PR MUST modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` (target match as above) AND STATUS.md MUST contain a row matching the standardised prefix `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` **with meaningful content** (format spec below). A bare-prefix stub row fails CI. (Closes 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 (safety) — bare-prefix stub bypass.)\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:47:   - **`cascade-status: blocked-on-adopter-conflict` (invariant-10 path):** PR MUST NOT modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` (no `enable-required-check.sh` invocation occurred — closing the bypass surface that R3 safety surfaced) AND MUST reference the filed `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` TF in DISPATCH-NOTE matching the standardised prefix **with meaningful content** (format spec below; bare-prefix stub fails CI per the same rule above).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:55:   The regex is **file-agnostic**: it matches the TF reference content, not the surrounding markdown (so the same line passes whether it has a `- **...**` STATUS.md bullet wrapper, lives in a DISPATCH-NOTE prose paragraph, or is otherwise embedded). The `(?:\\*\\*)?` optional group accepts the trailing `**` closing-bold marker that STATUS.md bullet format produces between the slug and the status parenthetical (closes 024A R7 R7-NEW-CRIT-001 — fix-round-6 dropped this and Example 1 silently failed its own regex). Concretely: `TF-024X-{type}-<adopter-slug>` (type ∈ {`renovate`, `conflict`}; adopter-slug is `<owner>-<repo>` lowercased, hyphens only), optionally followed by `**` (STATUS.md closing-bold), then ` ` (single space), parenthesised status ∈ {`(open)`, `(pending)`, `(in-progress)`, `(closed)`}, `: ` separator, then **≥20 characters starting with a non-whitespace character** (`\\S` anchor at start of description prevents all-whitespace bypass per R6 safety; `.{19,}` allows the remaining 19+ chars to be anything). `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (024B) implements this regex literally + greps for it across STATUS.md (operator-bump path) or DISPATCH-NOTE (conflict-close path) per the `cascade-status:` value.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:65:   The check is a hard predecessor for slice 024C — 024C does not open until the enforcement script is committed + green AND covers all four CI behaviours (the three named cascade-status check-paths + the fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised values). Closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 + 024A R2 NEW-MAJ-001 + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness — third cascade-status value) + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 (safety — bypass via concurrent invocation + conflict-declaration) + 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 (safety — bare-prefix TF-row stub bypass) + 024A R5 R5-NEW-MAJ-002 (safety — meaningful-content format spec) + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-001 (safety + completeness — regex non-whitespace anchor + file-agnostic scoping) + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-003 (safety — fail-closed default).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:66:3. **Cascade does NOT touch existing adopter content.** The wrapper is added; CODEOWNERS may gain a `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` line if the adopter has a CODEOWNERS file; nothing else in the adopter repo is modified by the cascade slice. Specifically: NOT the adopter's `README.md`, NOT `.github/workflows/*` other than the wrapper itself, NOT `package.json` / `pyproject.toml` / build config, NOT `.scp/rule-config.yaml` (the adopter writes that themselves once they need rule-level config).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:70:7. **Per-adopter rollback is single-operator-doable.** Each cascade slice ships a rollback procedure: `enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` reverts branch protection to the captured before-state, and the adopter wrapper PR can be reverted via standard `git revert`. Rollback time SLO: **<30 minutes from operator decision to merge-restored state — claimed only after slice 024B closes with a demonstrated real-repo round-trip on a throw-away test repo (not a dry-run mock).** The SLO is aspirational at 024A merge; 024B's acceptance criterion in §6 makes the round-trip a hard predecessor for 024C. Documented per cascade slice. Closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:89:- **Implementation slices (024B–024G)**: Opus orchestrator + Codex executor per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract. Each adopter cascade slice is a single PR _on the SCP repo_ shipping (a) the cascade slice's DISPATCH-NOTE with a `cascade-status:` field declaring one of three close-states per §5.2 + invariant 2, (b) the invocation-log entry under `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` **only when `cascade-status` is `onboarded` or `onboarded-operator-bump`** (when `cascade-status: blocked-on-adopter-conflict`, no log entry is added — the CI asserts log-file was NOT modified per invariant 2), (c) any SCP-side ADOPT-001 / scaffolder amendments. The adopter-side wrapper PR is a separate PR _on the adopter repo_, opened in parallel; the SCP-side cascade slice references the adopter PR URL. Closes 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 (correctness — §3 unconditional invocation-log claim contradicted invariant 2's conditional carve-out).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:128:   - `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` rendered by the scaffolder (024B), pinned to current SCP main HEAD SHA at slice-author time.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:129:   - Optional CODEOWNERS line `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml @<adopter-CODEOWNERS-account>` if the adopter has a CODEOWNERS file. If not, no CODEOWNERS work in cascade slice.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:132:   - `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/<slice-id>/DISPATCH-NOTE.md` (per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract). **MUST declare a `cascade-status:` field** in the DISPATCH-NOTE header taking one of **three** values:\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:135:     - **`blocked-on-adopter-conflict`** — invariant-10 conflict-close path; NO invocation occurred (conflict was discovered before invocation); a `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` TF is filed + referenced in DISPATCH-NOTE **with meaningful content per invariant 2's regex spec** (status field ∈ {open, pending, in-progress, closed} + description starting with a non-whitespace character (`\\S` anchor) + ≥20 chars total; bare-prefix stub or all-whitespace description fails CI); the PR MUST NOT modify `branch-protection-log.md` (CI script asserts absence of modification per invariant 2). Closes 024A R5 R5-NEW-MAJ-001 (completeness — §5.2 missing meaningful-content qualifier) + 024A R7 R7-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness) + R7-NEW-MAJ-003 (completeness) — `\\S` anchor + ≥20-char propagation to §5.2 paraphrase.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:137:     The `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI script (024B) parses this field and applies the appropriate check-path per invariant 2.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:138:   - `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` invocation log entry (D-035) — only when `cascade-status: onboarded` or `onboarded-operator-bump`.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:139:   - STATUS.md row update (cascade-slice progress) — and, when `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`, a `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row in \"Tracked-forward items\".\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:144:5. **FLA pilot safety findings reviewed** — single line in DISPATCH-NOTE (template lands in 024B's D-044): `FLA pilot safety findings reviewed: [none new since <last slice's check date> | <link to finding>]`. This is **not** an FLA precondition (invariant 4 still holds); it is a check that the cascade slice author has looked at the FLA pilot state before opening the slice, so safety discoveries don't silently accumulate between slices. Closes 024A R1 MIN-SAFE-005.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:146:### 5.3 Scaffolder helper (`SCP-073-scaffolder` = `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`, lands at 024B)\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:151:scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh \\\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:160:- `<output-dir>/.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` (the wrapper from `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl`, with substitutions for default-branch + scp-sha + scorecard-emit).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:164:D-044 ratifies this script's operational contract: bootstrap-only (refuses CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true per D-035 symmetry), validates `--scp-sha` against the SCP main HEAD at invocation time (warns if it's not main HEAD; refuses to emit if it's a non-existent SHA), and emits a manifest file `MANIFEST.json` listing every file emitted + its SHA256 for audit.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:171:- A `--restore <pre-state.json>` mode that consumes a captured before-state from a prior invocation log entry + reverses the branch-protection mutation (rollback path per invariant 7). Existing forward-mode behaviour unchanged.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:190:- ≥3 of {PIM, recommender, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower, shopify-app} have `policy-check / scp/policy-check` as a required status check on default branch (per `cascade-status: onboarded` or `onboarded-operator-bump`; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` adopters do NOT count until a successor sub-slice onboards them per invariant 10).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:192:- `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` is current (one entry per adopter that closed with `cascade-status: onboarded` or `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`; conflict-close slices have NO entry per invariant 2's negative assertion).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:206:| 024B | `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CI enforcement of invariant 2 — closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 + 024A R2 NEW-MAJ-001 + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 correctness + safety + 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 safety + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-002/003 safety) + scaffolder unit tests | Scaffolder emits a known-fixture wrapper that schema-validates against the canonical wrapper shape from ADOPT-001 §12; `--restore` round-trip via captured before-state restores branch-protection state byte-for-byte **on a real throw-away test repo** (not a dry-run mock — closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003); `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` parses DISPATCH-NOTE `cascade-status:` field and implements all four CI behaviours per invariant 2 — **fail-closed default** (absent or unrecognised value → exit non-zero); for `onboarded`: requires log entry + target match; for `onboarded-operator-bump`: requires log entry + target match + `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` STATUS.md row matching invariant 2's **regex format spec literally** (file-agnostic; `\\S` non-whitespace anchor at description start; ≥20 char total); for `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`: requires `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference (in DISPATCH-NOTE) matching the same regex spec literally AND **asserts log file was NOT modified** (closes the R3 safety bypass + R4 safety stub bypass + R6 safety regex/whitespace + file-scoping bypasses); D-044 filed. **All three components (scaffolder + --restore + check-invocation-log-entry.sh covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C.** | Codex executor | Per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:207:| 024C | PIM cascade — adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice (deliverables conditional on `cascade-status:` per §5.2 + invariant 2 — `onboarded`/`onboarded-operator-bump` paths ship invocation-log entry + post-bake observation; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` path ships `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference instead per invariant 10 with NO log entry; closes 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness — §6 024C/D/E/F rows now conditional on cascade-status — closes-marker per 024A R7 R7-NEW-MAJ-001 completeness)) | PIM `policy-check / scp/policy-check` required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean; D-045 filed. *(`blocked-on-adopter-conflict` close-state acceptance defers to invariant 10's sub-slice procedure; slice still merges with its conflict-TF + DISPATCH-NOTE record.)* | Codex executor + adopter PR | Per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:208:| 024D | control-tower cascade — adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice (same conditional-on-`cascade-status:` pattern as 024C) | control-tower `policy-check / scp/policy-check` required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean. *(No new D-NNN filed — D-045 at 024C ratifies the per-adopter onboarding contract pattern that this slice inherits unchanged.)* | Codex executor + adopter PR | Per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:209:| 024E | mapp-doc-agent + recommender paired cascade — both adopter PRs + SCP-side cascade slice (each adopter independently per §5.2 cascade-status spec; both `onboarded`/`onboarded-operator-bump` paths ship 2 invocation log entries + post-bake observations on both; conflict-close path on either adopter handled per invariant 10) | Both adopters' required-checks live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean on each. *(No new D-NNN filed — inherits D-045's pattern.)* | Codex executor + 2 adopter PRs | Per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:210:| 024F | shopify-app cascade — adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice (same conditional-on-`cascade-status:` pattern as 024C) | shopify-app `policy-check / scp/policy-check` required-check live; ≥1 Renovate-bump-propagation cycle merged clean. *(No new D-NNN filed — inherits D-045's pattern.)* | Codex executor + adopter PR | Per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:226:| **R-024-06** | A cohort adopter has a pre-existing `policy-check` workflow conflict. | T-024-10 mitigation: cascade slice CLOSES with status `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` per invariant 10 (forward TF `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` owned by the slice author; new sub-slice opens on conflict resolution). **CI enforcement (invariant 2):** when `cascade-status: blocked-on-adopter-conflict`, `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (a) verifies the `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference IS present in DISPATCH-NOTE **matching invariant 2's regex spec literally** (status field ∈ {open, pending, in-progress, closed} + description starting with a non-whitespace character (`\\S` anchor) + ≥20 chars total; bare-prefix stubs and all-whitespace descriptions fail CI) AND (b) **actively asserts that `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` was NOT modified in the PR diff** (closes the R3 safety bypass — a slice declaring conflict-close while actually invoking the script must fail CI). All three checks are required; positive evidence + regex-spec format match + negative assertion. Closes 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-001 (R-024-06 stale language flagged by all 3 lenses) + 024A R5 R5-NEW-MAJ-002 (completeness — meaningful-content qualifier) + 024A R7 R7-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness) + R7-NEW-MAJ-003 (completeness) — `\\S` anchor + ≥20-char propagation to R-024-06 paraphrase. | Each cascade slice |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:227:| **R-024-07** | Renovate misses a cohort adopter (e.g. adopter has Renovate disabled). | The cascade slice surfaces this in DISPATCH-NOTE by declaring `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`. Operator-driven SHA pin bump PR is acceptable as a **temporary** unblock, but the cascade slice MUST file a forward TF (`TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>`) **as a STATUS.md \"Tracked-forward items\" row matching invariant 2's regex spec literally** (status field ∈ {open, pending, in-progress, closed} + description starting with a non-whitespace character (`\\S` anchor) + ≥20 chars total — bare-prefix stubs and all-whitespace descriptions fail the CI check per invariant 2; closes 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 safety + 024A R7 R7-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness) + R7-NEW-MAJ-003 (completeness) — pre-R6 paraphrase swept at R-024-07). The `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI script verifies STATUS.md contains the matching TF row + regex-spec match when DISPATCH-NOTE declares `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`. The adopter is **not credited toward Threshold A** until that TF closes + a real Renovate cycle has merged + observed clean. This distinguishes adopters that genuinely exercise automated version-skew tolerance from those that satisfy the letter of the criterion via a one-off operator action. Closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-004 + 024A R2 NEW-MIN-002 + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness — third cascade-status value enumerated) + 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 (safety — meaningful-content gate). T-024-04 mitigation still applies. | Each cascade slice |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:233:| **R-024-13** | Plan-doc commits to scaffolder shape before scaffolder is implemented. | Plan-doc is v0.1. Scaffolder's ratifying decision (D-044) lands at 024B with the implementation. Plan-doc shape may be amended at 024B if implementation surfaces a better shape. | 024A → 024B |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:235:| **R-024-15** | An adopter accepted into the cascade then later wants to opt out. | Invariant 7: per-adopter rollback is single-operator-doable + <30min SLO. The adopter's `enable-required-check.sh --restore` invocation reverts branch-protection; the wrapper PR can be reverted via `git revert`. Documented per cascade slice. | Each cascade slice |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:242:- D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reserved (not assigned in this slice).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:246:- Each adopter that reached `cascade-status: onboarded` or `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump` has a corresponding entry in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` with operator + timestamp + before/after API JSON + script SHA256 + git SHA. Adopters whose cascade slice closed with `cascade-status: blocked-on-adopter-conflict` have NO log entry (per invariant 2's negative assertion) and do NOT count toward Threshold A's \"≥3 of 5\" criterion until a successor sub-slice onboards them per invariant 10.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:259:| **D-044** | 024B | `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` operational contract — bootstrap-only / no-CI guards (D-035 symmetry); `--scp-sha` validation against SCP main HEAD; `--default-branch` flag + template substitution; `MANIFEST.json` audit emission. Adopter-template versioning (template SHA captured in scaffolder output for forensic traceability). Invocation-log convention extension: scaffolder writes a \"rendered-template\" log entry alongside `enable-required-check.sh`'s branch-protection log. Ratifies invariants 2 + 3 + 10 in code form. |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:263:**Codex-executor reservation guard.** Per the `docs/DECISIONS.md` header reservation block, Codex executors dispatched for any WP-SCP-024 implementation slice must NOT assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that slice. The reservation pattern mirrors WP-SCP-022's D-021 reservation guard + WP-SCP-023's D-041/D-042/D-043 reservation guard.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:271:3. **`enable-required-check.sh --restore` test surface** — the rollback mode lands at 024B. How is it tested without actually mutating an estate repo? **Resolution path (closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003):** Q3 closes only when 024B's acceptance criterion in §6 is met — i.e. a real-repo round-trip on a throw-away test repo (NOT a dry-run mock). Until that demonstration is complete, invariant 7's <30-min rollback SLO is aspirational and 024C MUST NOT open.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
