{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1118,1188p' docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,10p' docs/DECISIONS.md && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '88,102p' docs/DECISIONS.md && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,6p' STATUS.md && printf '\\\\n---\\\\n' && sed -n '118,150p' STATUS.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n#### Reference\n\n- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-022 (federation-primitive adoption); D-029 (`statuses: write` for readback); D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection); D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account); D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-check); D-033 (rendered context-name `policy-check / scp/policy-check`); D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection); D-035 (020G adopter-helper invocation); D-036 (`policies/VERSIONING.md` semver contract + rule-RFC process as estate doctrine; closes 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5); D-040 (slice 020L: 48h is CEILING-not-FLOOR in single-operator mode for the rule-RFC process); D-041 (cross-repo scorecard data shape, opt-in adopter participation); D-042 (aggregator pipeline trust model + mandatory `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`); D-043 (MCP `scp.consult_scorecard` read-only contract); D-044 (WP-SCP-024 024B scaffolder + `--restore` + invocation-log CI).\n- `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` for the full federation-primitive spec.\n- `docs/plans/WP-SCP-023-cross-repo-scorecards.md` for the full cross-repo scorecard plan.\n- `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/RULE-001-waiver-reason-must-cite-issue-or-pr.md` (post-v1.1.0) — canonical specification for SCP-R-004.\n- `docs/security/branch-protection.md` for the SCP-side protection state.\n- §11.10 of this document for the `.scp/rule-config.yaml` CODEOWNERS recommendation referenced from §12.7.4.\n\n#### 12.7.15 Cross-repo scorecard opt-in (post-WP-SCP-023 / v1.2.0)\n\nAdopters MAY opt in to cross-repo scorecard aggregation. This is **optional**; non-participating repos see no behaviour change and are NOT listed as \"non-compliant\" anywhere — invariant 4 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc.\n\n**Privacy contract:** the emit aggregator carries **aggregated counts only** — never `reason`, `approved_by`, or `waiver_id` strings from your `output/findings/waivers.json`. Schema (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json`) enforces `additionalProperties: false` at every level. The aggregator NEVER reads your sibling waiver content directly; it consumes only the per-PR `scorecard-emit.json` artifact your wrapper publishes.\n\n**Three steps to opt in:**\n\n1. **Bump your wrapper's SHA pin to v1.2.0 or later.** Renovate will prompt automatically; merge as you would any other SCP version bump.\n\n2. **Set `scorecard-emit: true`** on your wrapper's `with:` block AND grant the two extra permissions the called `attest-scorecard` job needs:\n   ```yaml\n   permissions:\n     contents: read\n     statuses: write\n     attestations: write   # required by called attest-scorecard job\n     id-token: write       # required for OIDC artifact attestation\n   jobs:\n     policy-check:\n       uses: jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<sha>\n       with:\n         scorecard-emit: true   # opt-in; default false\n   ```\n   Default-false (no `with:` block at all) means existing wrappers continue to work unchanged with the original two-permission ceiling. **You only add `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` if you opt in** — reusable workflows can never escalate above the caller's permission ceiling, so without these two the workflow fails at startup. The called workflow's `attest-scorecard` job is JOB-SCOPED on these permissions (closes WP-SCP-023 023B R1 MAJ-SAFE-001), so opt-out runs never request an OIDC token even if you grant them at the wrapper level.\n\n   > **Repo visibility / ownership prerequisite (TF-023E-001).** GitHub's `actions/attest-build-provenance` rejects user-owned private repos with HTTP error `Feature not available for user-owned private repositories`. Your repo MUST be either (a) public, or (b) owned by an organisation. If neither applies, the attestation step will fail and your runs will not produce a verifiable emit. The aggregator records repos without a verifiable attestation as `verification_failure` (per D-042 trust model); they are NOT silently accepted.\n\n3. **PR an entry to `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml`** in this repo:\n   ```yaml\n   - repo: \"<your-owner>/<your-repo>\"\n     default_branch: \"main\"\n     expected_scp_workflow_ref: \"jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<the-same-sha>\"\n     opted_in_at: \"2026-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ\"\n   ```\n   The `expected_scp_workflow_ref` is what the aggregator passes to `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`. **It MUST match the SHA your wrapper pins.** When you bump the SHA pin, update this entry in the same PR (or a sibling PR before the next aggregator run) — a mismatch records as `verification_failure` in the index, NOT silent acceptance.\n\n**How to read your data:**\n\n- **Markdown report:** `docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` is rendered weekly. The aggregator opens a PR for operator review on the SCP repo each Monday; the report lands on `main` once @jrnb2024 reviews and merges.\n- **Central index:** `output/scorecards/index.json` carries the canonical machine-readable shape; schema at `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`.\n- **MCP method:** `scp.consult_scorecard` (per D-043) returns aggregated metrics + verification status. Optional filters: `repo_filter` (single repo) and `since_emitted_at` (ISO-8601). Read-only — no mutation surface.\n\n**Common failure modes you may see in the index:**\n\n| Status | Cause | Remediation |\n|---|---|---|\n| `verified` | OIDC verification + schema validation succeeded. | None. |\n| `verification_failure` | `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` failed (SHA pin mismatch in `expected_scp_workflow_ref`) OR emit schema validation failed. | Update your registry entry's `expected_scp_workflow_ref` to match your wrapper's pinned SHA. |\n| `unreachable` | The aggregator could not reach your repo (rate limit, deletion, transient API error). | If transient, the next weekly run should recover. The aggregator retains the prior verified row's data alongside the unreachable status when available. |\n| `no_emit` | No green policy-check run on default branch within last 7 days OR run had no `scorecard-emit` artifact. | Confirm `scorecard-emit: true` is on your wrapper; confirm your default branch's policy-check is green. |\n\n**Verifying a downloaded emit on your side:**\n\n```bash\ngh run download <run-id> --repo <your-owner>/<your-repo> --name scorecard-emit\ngh attestation verify scorecard-emit/scorecard-emit.json \\\n  --signer-workflow jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<sha>\n```\n\n**Opt-out:** delete your row from `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` via PR. The next aggregator run will not include you. You can also turn off `scorecard-emit: true` in your wrapper independently.\n\n\n---\n# Standards Control Plane — Decision Log\n\n**Last Updated:** 2026-05-09 (D-044 filed at WP-SCP-024 024B; D-045 / D-046 remain reserved; estate cascade)\n\n> **D-021 reservation note (2026-04-28):** D-021 is reserved for the\n> 2026-05-31 atomic workday filing per WP-SCP-019 hygiene response (PR\n> #30, 2026-04-21). Codex executors running WP-SCP-022 implementation\n> slices must NOT assign D-021 to any decision filed during the\n> autonomous run. The WP-SCP-022 §4.7 gate-enforcement helper\n> (`scripts/wp_scp_022_gate_check.sh --check-d021`) detects collisions.\n\n---\n| D-041 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B (this PR). The schema defines aggregated per-rule counts (raw_findings, denies, waived, rule_config_disabled), waivers aggregate (active_count, by_rule_id, expiring_within_30d), rule-config aggregate (disabled_rules, expiring_within_30d), repo / ref / commit / scp_version / RFC3339 emitted_at, and a verdict (allow/deny/warn). The schema EXPLICITLY DOES NOT include waiver content (`reason`, `approved_by`, `waiver_id` strings) — invariant 2 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc binds this. The reusable workflow gains a `scorecard-emit: bool` `workflow_call` input (default false) so existing adopters see no behaviour change; opt-in adopters set `with: scorecard-emit: true`. Schema versioning: MAJOR-pinned per `policies/VERSIONING.md` D-036 + WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1 — aggregator drops emits with unknown `schema_version`. Verification: GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation (OIDC-based) via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0` (SHA `a2bbfa25...`) at emit time; aggregator verifies via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` (per D-042 to be filed at slice 023C). v1.2.0 cut on this slice's merge per VERSIONING.md MINOR category | ACCEPTED | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety property: existing adopters cannot have new behaviour spring on them; opt-in is explicit per invariant 4. The waiver-content exclusion (invariant 2) is enforced by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` constraint on every level + the explicit field enumeration. The MAJOR-pinning posture means schema breakage requires v2.0.0 + adopter migration; v0.1 prefix on `schema_version` reflects the freedom to amend until first adopter opts in. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation |\n| D-042 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C (this PR). Mechanism: per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (the GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation OIDC pattern, mandatory per the D-042 reservation note above + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits (slice 020J) + `output/scorecards/** @jrnb2024` CODEOWNERS coverage (slice 023A) + branch protection on main (slice 020D2), NOT a separate Ed25519 key layer. The aggregator runs as `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` on a weekly cron (Monday 06:00 UTC) + `workflow_dispatch`; two-job structure (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped via job-level permissions, mirroring the 023B `attest-scorecard` job split); reads `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` (CODEOWNERS-protected at `docs/scorecards/**`), pulls each adopter's latest green policy-check run's `scorecard-emit.json` artifact, verifies attestation, schema-validates emit, aggregates into `output/scorecards/index.json` (schema: `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`), and opens a PR for operator review. Failure modes (verification_failure / unreachable / no_emit) record loudly per-adopter — never silently dropped. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema `additionalProperties: false` at every level). Internal-only workflow per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\"Scope\" (mirrors 020N conflict-gate.yml posture); no semver bump. Verifies WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 6 (\"Aggregator output is Ed25519-signed\") in spirit — Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub rather than by an SCP-side private key, eliminating the private-key-distribution surface | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 (per-emit data shape + opt-in model) — D-041 ratified the EMITTER side of the trust model; D-042 ratifies the AGGREGATOR / VERIFIER side. The mandatory `--signer-workflow` constraint was already pre-committed at the D-042 reservation note above (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001) — this slice ratifies it as workflow code. The Ed25519-via-Sigstore framing eliminates the chicken-and-egg of \"where does the SCP private key live and how does the aggregator hold it without exposing adopters\" — GitHub manages the keys via OIDC + Sigstore. The two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) is identical to 023B's `policy-check` + `attest-scorecard` split (closes the analogous threat surface where workflow-level write permissions could be exploited by a compromised aggregate-side step). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure |\n| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B operational contracts for cascade scaffolding (this PR). Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (= `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically — bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments `--adopter-repo`, `--default-branch`, `--scp-sha`, `--scorecard-emit`, `--output-dir` per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12; future wrapper-shape changes land in the template + propagate via Renovate SHA bumps. (3) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` mode reverses prior branch-protection mutation from a captured before-state per plan-doc invariant 7 (rollback SLO <30 min single-operator-doable). New safety check (forward mode only): refuses to invoke against a target whose `policy-check / scp/policy-check` check has not run successfully on a recent PR — closes the foot-gun where an operator could enable required-check on an adopter whose wrapper PR is still pending; `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag for cold-start scenarios. (4) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI enforces invariant 2's 4 cascade-status check behaviours: fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; `onboarded` requires log entry + target match; `onboarded-operator-bump` additionally requires STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` requires DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex literally + log file NOT modified. Regex (Python re): `TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open|pending|in-progress|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` — matches in STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE; `\\S` anchor at description start prevents all-whitespace bypass; ≥20 chars total. (5) ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure — 3-gate playbook (disable via `--restore` → SHA-pin to last known-good release tag → re-enable after Renovate-bumped fix). All four script components (scaffolder + `--restore` + `--i-understand` flag + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C. Slice 024B itself ships under documented protocol deviation (direct codex exec / claude -p; non-kernel-dangerous shell + tests + docs scope) per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md` note + justify rule; 024C entry is conditional on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure (per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04) per the §9 reservation block; this slice ratifies it. The four-component scope (scaffolder + template + `--restore` + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh`) is the single hardest predecessor surface for cohort cascade — without all four, cascade slices 024C-F would each rebuild the per-adopter wrapper shape, the rollback procedure, and the cascade-status invariant enforcement from scratch (multiplying the 9-round adversarial-review burden that 024A absorbed by 4 cohort slices). The `MANIFEST.json` + SHA256 audit surface mirrors the `install_acc_hook.sh` pattern (atomic config + binary SHA pinning) — provides forensic traceability for cascade-driven adopter-side artefact authorship. The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag closes the cold-start chicken-and-egg: a new adopter has no green CI before the wrapper merges + at least one PR runs, so the safety check would otherwise block first-onboard; the explicit flag is the operator's acknowledgement that they accept the cold-start risk for that single first-onboard run. The break-glass 3-gate procedure is intentionally NOT a one-button kill-switch (all gates auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures adopters don't stay un-gated forever). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation. |\n\n---\n# Standards Control Plane — STATUS\n\n**Last updated:** 2026-05-09 (WP-SCP-024 024B - scaffolder + --restore + invocation-log CI; D-044 filed; previous: 2026-05-09 D-035-rules retired)\n\n## At-a-glance\n\n\n---\n| 5 | #101 | **023E** | WP-SCP-023 Threshold A scaffolding (closes TF-023D-003 + TF-023A-002; **defers TF-023C-001 → TF-023E-001 + TF-023E-002**). NEW `docs/gates/USER-GATE-D.md` (status: `not-yet-signed`) — 8-criterion checklist for operator sign-off when ≥3 adopters (FLA mandatory) opted in + first weekly aggregator clean. Closed TF-023D-003: `_log_tool_invocation` now reads active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` via new `_resolve_audit_key_id()` helper (graceful fallback `key-ring-unreadable` if key ring empty/malformed; never blocks tool calls). Updated `test_stdio_handshake.py` expected tools list to include `consult_scorecard`. 86/86 MCP tests pass. **fix-round-3:** Two real CI gaps surfaced — (1) SCP-self opt-in attempted then reverted because GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos (filed TF-023E-001). (2) Wrapper SHA pin bump (v1.0.0 → @5ff2acd) reverted because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation), and the `attest-scorecard` job's `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` exceed the wrapper's ceiling — startup_failure even with `scorecard-emit: false` (filed TF-023E-002 — restructure policy-check.yml so attest-scorecard is a separate top-level workflow file). USER-GATE-D criterion (i) updated: SCP-self carve-out — satisfied set is now `FLA + ≥2 of {PIM / recommender / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower}`. R1/R2 adversarial review missed both constraints (only visible at actual CI runtime in this repo's specific visibility/ownership context). Wrapper stays pinned at v1.0.0 (@41a5299) until TF-023E-002 closes. Merged at `295e0da`. |\n| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — D-035-rules retired + WP-SCP-025 parked)\n\n**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\n\n**The 6 retired rule names** (preserved here for traceability — re-evaluate at WP-SCP-025 kickoff against the §4 candidate list in the parked plan-doc):\n1. `sdk_version_pin` (was Wave 1 gate)\n2. `ct_sdk_conformance` (was Wave 1 gate)\n3. `sdk_migration_waiver` (was Wave 1 gate)\n4. `sdk_adoption_schedule` (was Wave 1 mid)\n5. `bff_refresh_hardening` (was Wave 2 gate)\n6. `ct_auth_provider_memoization` (was Wave 3 gate)\n\n**Cross-project reconciliation:** SCP filed `SCP-D035-RULES-RETIRED-2026-05-09.md` to CT governance notifications log requesting CT amendments to (a) `docs/briefings/recommender-shopify-j1-rbac-response-2026-05-09.md` Q6+Q8 to drop the 6-rules / 2026-05-15-deadline framing before the response ships, (b) `docs/plans/PLAN-CT-D-rollout.md` §3 WP-D-SCP entry to point at WP-SCP-025 backlog. CT-owned changes; SCP requesting explicitly so cross-project view stays consistent.\n\n**Forward work:** WP-SCP-025 (`docs/plans/WP-SCP-025-domain-rules-v1.md`) parked with 5 candidate rules (protected_tables_updated_with_migration / r1_evidence_linked_in_pr_body / waiver_expiry_within_window / secrets_not_in_committed_env_files / permission_schema_registered_within_wave_window) for WP-SCP-025 owner to review and pick 2-3 from at scoping time. Owner: TBD (named at parked-plan kickoff post-024 Threshold A).\n\n**Slice 024B remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope unchanged: scaffolder + `--restore` mode + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + D-044 + real-repo rollback round-trip.\n\n## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — slice 024B + protocol-deviation-noted)\n\n| # | PR | Slice | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #<scaffolder-PR> | **024B** | D-044 filed; protocol deviation noted (direct codex exec for 024B; cohort cascade 024C-F gated on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure); plan-doc §6 amended with cohort dispatcher precondition; ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure shipped; scaffolder + template + `--restore` + invocation-log CI + tests all live; `--restore` real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md`. |\n\n## Open PRs (post-Threshold-A session close-out)\n\n- **PR #59** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/deliberate-violation-pre`; permanent fixture; CI=FAIL by design (deny); blocked structurally by required-check.\n- **PR #67** 🔄 OPEN (DO-NOT-MERGE) — `canary/waived-violation`; permanent fixture; CI=PASS via waiver suppression; label-only protection (TF-020H4-002 covers).\n- **PR #81** 🔄 OPEN (